WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.020
Think areas, not promises.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:05.426
Support is an area where buying previously slowed a fall.

3
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.054
Resistance is where selling slowed a rise.

4
00:00:08.583 --> 00:00:10.418
Notice repeated reactions.

5
00:00:10.538 --> 00:00:17.004
If price repeatedly turns near $100 or $110, mark those areas to study.

6
00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:18.703
A level can break.

7
00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:21.679
A past reaction does not guarantee another.

8
00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:23.726
Price can move through either area.

9
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.748
Check the wider picture.

10
00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:27.714
Compare the trend and timeframe.

11
00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:30.562
A chart pattern alone is not a reason to enter.

12
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:32.488
Practice a decision.

13
00:00:32.608 --> 00:00:37.566
In the Chart lab, describe what you see and plan a possible loss before choosing an entry.

